The Heat seem to understand the importance of having a good bench, and it shows as they have two of the highest bench scoring seasons of the past 20 years. The Mavs also benefited from having a strong bench when they beat the Heat in 2011 to win the championship. In fact, besides the 2009 Cavaliers, every single team on this list at least made it to the playoffs, 5 made it to the championship, and 3 won the title (Heat 2006, Mavs 2011, and Spurs 2007). However, this list doesn’t show the most recent champions. Meaning that bench production isn’t essential to bring home championships in the modern era.
So even though the production of bench points has gone down significantly, and bench points don’t necessarily mean better chances at winning a championship recently, it is still true that teams have more sustained success over time if their bench can pitch in every now and then.
